4|0@medicalschool^1440651633#cuh5mzi:[deleted]$:Why are you interested in IM as opposed to FM? There are further things you can do past a FM residency that you can research. And I feel like you should look at the silver lining. There are IMGs and FMGs with better scores than you that have less of a chance of even matching. Be fortunate of your position and understand that a lower than average board score doesn't mean you're a failure. Not to be a tough ass but you just got to suck it up and be happy with the opportunities you still have. Anyone can fail an exam, hell I have before. But when years pass, you look back and realize that one or two tests you took in the past and had anxiety over, do NOT matter anymore.
